  "content": {
    "en": {
      "overviewMd": "By the end of this unit, **we** will be able to:\n\n1. **Make plans with friends** using time expressions and days of the week.\n2. **Tell and understand time** (What time is it? At what time?).\n3. **Use the verb \"moći\" (can)** to ask if someone is available.\n4. **Use the verb \"piti\" (to drink)** to order drinks and sociali",
      "grammarMd": "## 3. Grammar (Gramatika)\n\n### A. Days of the Week - Planning Ahead\n\nThe days of the week are essential for making plans. In Serbian, the week starts on Monday.\n\n#### Days of the Week\n\n| Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Ponedeljak* | Monday |\n| Utorak | Tuesday |\n| Sreda | Wednesday |\n| Četvrtak* | Thursday |\n| Petak | Friday |\n| Subota | Saturday |\n| Nedelja* | Sunday |\n\n*Montenegro: Ponedeljak, Četvrtak, Nedelja (same)\n\n#### Using Days in Sentences\n\nTo say \"**on Monday**,\" use **\"u ponedeljak\"** (literally: \"in Monday\").\n\n**Examples:**\n*   **U ponedeljak idem u grad.** (On Monday I'm going to town.)\n*   **Možeš li u petak?** (Can you on Friday?)\n*   **Vidimo se u subotu.** (See you on Saturday.)\n\n---\n\n### B. Telling Time (Koliko je sati?)\n\nTelling time is crucial for making plans and meeting friends.\n\n#### Basic Time Questions\n\n| Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Koliko je sati? | What time is it? |\n| Sada je... | It is now... |\n| U koliko sati? | At what time? |\n| U... sati. | At... o'clock. |\n\n#### Hours (1-12)\n\n| Time | Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1:00 | Jedan sat | One o'clock |\n| 2:00 | Dva sata | Two o'clock |\n| 3:00 | Tri sata | Three o'clock |\n| 4:00 | Četiri sata | Four o'clock |\n| 5:00 | Pet sati | Five o'clock |\n| 6:00 | Šest sati | Six o'clock |\n| 7:00 | Sedam sati | Seven o'clock |\n| 8:00 | Osam sati | Eight o'clock |\n| 9:00 | Devet sati | Nine o'clock |\n| 10:00 | Deset sati | Ten o'clock |\n| 11:00 | Jedanaest sati | Eleven o'clock |\n| 12:00 | Dvanaest sati | Twelve o'clock |\n\n**Note:** The word \"sat\" (hour) changes form:\n*   1 sat\n*   2-4 sata\n*   5+ sati\n\n#### Half Hours\n\nTo say \"half past,\" use **\"pola\"** (half) + the **next hour**.\n\n**Examples:**\n*   **Pola šest** = 5:30 (literally: \"half six\")\n*   **Pola osam** = 7:30 (literally: \"half eight\")\n\n#### Time of Day\n\n| Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Ujutru | In the morning |\n| Popodne* | In the afternoon |\n| Uveče* | In the evening |\n| Noću | At night |\n\n*Montenegro: Popodne (same), Uveče (same)\n\n---\n\n### C. Verb \"moći\" (can / to be able to)\n\nThe verb **\"moći\"** is essential for asking if someone is available or able to do something.\n\n#### Conjugation Table\n\n| Person | Serbian | English |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Ja** | mogu | I can |\n| **Ti** | možeš | You can (informal) |\n| **On/Ona/Ono** | može | He/She/It can |\n| **Mi** | možemo | We can |\n| **Vi** | možete | You can (formal/plural) |\n| **Oni/One/Ona** | mogu | They can |\n\n#### Practical Examples\n\n*   **Mogu li da dođem?** (Can I come?)\n*   **Možeš li večeras?** (Can you tonight?)\n*   **Ne mogu sutra.** (I can't tomorrow.)\n*   **Možemo da se nađemo.** (We can meet.)\n*   **Ona može u petak.** (She can on Friday.)\n\n---\n\n### D. Verb \"piti\" (to drink)\n\nThe verb **\"piti\"** is essential for ordering drinks and sociali",
      "phrasesMd": "## 4. Phrases (Practical Application)\n\nThis section combines our new vocabulary and grammar into real-world phrases and dialogues about going out with friends.\n\n### A. Essential Phrases for Making Plans\n\n| Situation | Serbian Phrase | English Translation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Asking if someone is free | Slobodan si? / Slobodna si? | Are you free? (m/f) |\n| Asking what someone is doing | Šta radiš večeras? | What are you doing tonight? |\n| Saying you're free | Slobodan sam. / Slobodna sam. | I'm free. (m/f) |\n| Saying you're busy | Zau",
      "dialoguesMd": "",
      "testIntroductionMd": "**We** will use these exercises to solidify our understanding of making plans, telling time, and sociali"
    }
  },
